        "id": 98827,
        "name": "Julia",
        "username": "Julia",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/j/2bfe46/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-04-07T21:59:22.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Pwatson1974 ran the first Sentinels game I ever played in, and forever shall I remain grateful for it. This was back in the 1st Edition days, about a month before Rook City came out. The game was Citizen Dawn in Atlantis. I believe we had Tempest, Visionary and Ra already at the table, and I chose Fanatic, because she looked so very badass with her wings armour and sword and all that.</p><p>I had the obligatory 'Why am I hitting myself?' moment, but then I understood that, while Fanatic may go down (in flames!), she will make damn sure that the villains go down with her! From that point onwards I had so much fun that she became my go-to character for a while.</p><p>As for my first game, I believe we all got our butts kicked by the Kraken in the end, but I didn't mind at all. I spent the next two weeks tracking down my own copy of the game, and the rest is history (and I can't believe that it has only been two years!).</p>",
        "post_number": 21,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:26:35.961Z",
