      {
        "id": 98829,
        "name": "grysqrl",
        "username": "grysqrl",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/grysqrl/{size}/1909_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-04-08T12:42:24.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I played Wraith along with one other person who didn't know how to play, taught by a third person who appeared very knowledgeable but, it later turned out, had never played before. We stomped on Omnitron in Silver Gulch, only to figure out later that Omnitron probably should have flipped over at some point (i.e. every round). We followed it up with two two-player games against Apostate with heroes who had little chance at getting through the DR once his relics were set up (I don't remember them all, but Scholar and Expat were in the mix).</p><p>Then I immediately grabbed up everything I could and actually learned how to play.</p>",
