      {
        "id": 98832,
        "name": "charlotteML",
        "username": "charlotteML",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/e19adc/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-04-15T07:49:53.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>When I first played the guy who owned the game (everything including promos up to Vengance at that point) had laid out all the heroes, villains and environments to let us have a look and I instantly noticed Unity, mostly due to her being a brunette with what I thought would be some type of engineering/technical skills. We ended up playing a five player game against Dawn (Owner as Ra, me as Unity, other completely new player as eternal Haka, someone else I can't remember what they played and then Ab Zero)</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I enjoyed Unity throughout the game (I think her art and flavour text is what made me fall in love with the game) and we did end up winning although I think our team work left a little to be desired (me playing mr chomps the round before Haka did a rampage, a player who killed off one of the citizens when we were trying to get Dawn to flip back. Also a first round quote from the owner of the game: \"Wait, you three ALL picked the version of your heroes who can't deal damage?! Hmmm, ok...\") I didn't quite get a chance to set up a huge amount of damage but did contribute consistently throughout the game.</p>",
        "post_number": 26,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:26:36.357Z",
