      {
        "id": 98836,
        "name": "TeslaRoyale",
        "username": "TeslaRoyale",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/t/9fc29f/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-04-21T04:30:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>My first game was with Reckless, Nielzabub, and Rapscalion back in original edition. They had played a couple games already so I asked what hero they didn't like because I was used to playing games with people who alway played the same characters or same group position.&nbsp; I figured that way I wouldn't have to compete with people for heroes in future games.&nbsp; They told me Visionary wasn't very good.&nbsp; I took her, and shuffled her deck, as we prepared to square off with Omnitron.&nbsp; I quickly came to like her deck control and then an \"Electro Pulse Explosive\" happened.&nbsp; Everyone dropped what they had planned for their turns and started discussing what they could do to get DR or damage it.&nbsp; I just looked down at my hand and see this card called \"Wrest the Mind\" that I had been reading for half the game trying to figure out what a target was and why I would ever want to take that much damage of my own for anything.&nbsp; (When we first started we were really conservative with hit points and almost revered DR as the holy grail of effects.)&nbsp; I just said, \"Guys, I got this.\"&nbsp; I throw it on the \"Electro Pulse.\"&nbsp; Reckless pulls out his Kindle and jumps on the forums to check that it was a legal move.&nbsp; Then we go through the round and when the villian turn comes up he asks, \"Alright so you want to redirect it the explosive and blow it up.\"&nbsp; To which I respond with, \"No, I want to hit Omnitron.\"&nbsp; I hit Omnitron. Then he explains to me how the damage on \"Wrest the Mind\" works like an interupt and asks me if I want to redirect the next hit to the \"Expolsive\" and he tells me I will take some total amount of damage that I can't actually remember off the top of my head (I can't remember how many heroes we were using.)&nbsp; I respond with, \"It's a three to one damage exchange rate!&nbsp; I will gladly take that.\"&nbsp; And from then on she has always been one of or depending on the day my favorite character.  <img src=\"//forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slightly_smiling_face.png?v=9\" title=\":slightly_smiling_face:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slightly_smiling_face:\"></p>",
